.TE
.sp
Note: \fB\-\-decrypt=stash\fP requires write access to the database.
Otherwise, \fBnotmuch show\fP operates entirely in read\-only mode.
.sp
Default: \fBauto\fP
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-exclude=(true|false)
Specify whether to omit threads only matching search.exclude_tags
from the search results (the default) or not. In either case the
excluded message will be marked with the exclude flag (except when
output=mbox when there is nowhere to put the flag).
.sp
If \fB\-\-entire\-thread\fP is specified then complete threads are returned
regardless (with the excluded flag being set when appropriate) but
threads that only match in an excluded message are not returned
when \fB\-\-exclude=true.\fP
.sp
The default is \fB\-\-exclude=true.\fP
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-body=(true|false)
If true (the default) \fBnotmuch show\fP includes the bodies of the
messages in the output; if false, bodies are omitted.
\fB\-\-body=false\fP is only implemented for the text, json and sexp
formats and it is incompatible with \fB\-\-part > 0.\fP
.sp
This is useful if the caller only needs the headers as body\-less
output is much faster and substantially smaller.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-include\-html
Include \(dqtext/html\(dq parts as part of the output (currently
only supported with \fB\-\-format=text\fP, \fB\-\-format=json\fP and
\fB\-\-format=sexp\fP). By default, unless \fB\-\-part=N\fP is used to
select a specific part or \fB\-\-include\-html\fP is used to include all
\(dqtext/html\(dq parts, no part with content type \(dqtext/html\(dq is included
in the output.
.UNINDENT
.sp
A common use of \fBnotmuch show\fP is to display a single thread of
email messages. For this, use a search term of \(dqthread:<thread\-id>\(dq as
can be seen in the first column of output from the
notmuch\-search \%<#\:notmuch-search-1> command.
.SH "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
.sp
Structured output (json / sexp) is influenced by the configuration
option show.extra_headers \%<#\:nmconfig-show\:.extra_headers>\&. See
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1> for details.
.SH "وضعیت خروج (EXIT STATUS)"
.sp
This command supports the following special exit status codes
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB20\fP
The requested format version is too old.
.TP
.B \fB21\fP
The requested format version is too new.
.UNINDENT
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
notmuch \%<#\:notmuch-1>,
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1>,
notmuch\-count \%<#\:notmuch-count-1>,
notmuch\-dump \%<#\:notmuch-dump-1>,
notmuch\-hooks \%<#\:notmuch-hooks-5>,
notmuch\-insert \%<#\:notmuch-insert-1>,
notmuch\-new \%<#\:notmuch-new-1>,
notmuch\-reply \%<#\:notmuch-reply-1>,
notmuch\-restore \%<#\:notmuch-restore-1>,
notmuch\-search \%<#\:notmuch-search-1>,
notmuch\-search\-terms \%<#\:notmuch-search-terms-7>,
notmuch\-tag \%<#\:notmuch-tag-1>
